NP.TXT:
This reference was made in the course of proceedings between G. Pohl-Boskamp GmbH & Co. KG (
          Pohl-Boskamp
          ) and the Gemeinsamer Bundesausschuss (Joint Federal Committee) regarding the latter's refusal to include two ready-to-use medicinal products belonging to the applicant in the main proceedings on a list of non-prescription medicinal products which can, by way of exception, be prescribed and thus covered by the compulsory health insurance scheme.

The statutory provisions governing the compulsory health insurance scheme in Germany are set out, in essence, in Book V of the German Social Law Code (Sozialgesetzbuch,
              the SGB V
              ).
